/*
 * dns_diag_codes.h - the message codes of karicheck (X-macro list, one code per line).
 *
 *   X (ID, "area.subject[.detail]", severity, "one-line description")    a code in use
 *   XR(ID, "area.subject[.detail]", severity, "one-line description")    a retired code: nothing prints it any more, the name stays reserved
 *
 * severity is the default one: 'E' error, 'W' warning, 'N' note, 'I' info.  A check whose severity the configuration sets (check-*
 * options) prints the code with the severity in force; the JSON output of karicheck carries the severity of the message itself.
 *
 * Rules (planning file 0.6.x karicheck --json, section 4):
 *  - A code names the problem, not the message text: one code may have several texts, and a text may change without its code.
 *  - A code is never renamed and never reused for another problem once released.  A code that is no longer printed becomes XR().
 *  - ID is the name in capitals with '.' and '-' written as '_' (tests/check_diag_codes.pl checks it).
 *  - Keep one entry per line, in this form: the docs list (docs/karicheck.md) is generated from this file and checked against it.
 *  - Areas: usage, io, conf, zone, db, internal.
 */

